  "description": "Construction of a mansard roof extension with front and rear facing dormer windows. Construction of a first floor rear extension. Subdivision of split level first/ second floor flat to facilitate the creation of self contained 1 x 1 bedroom first floor flat and 1 x 1 studio within roof space (Use Class C3).",
  "epc_number": null,
  "ward": "Lea Bridge",
  "last_updated": "2026-11-18T11:32:11.394Z",
  "street_name": "HOE STREET",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed second floor flat, by reason of its restricted floor to ceiling height, would provide an inadequate standard of residential accommodation for future occupiers. 4.2 sq.m, equivalent to 9.5% of its 44.2 sq.m gross internal area, would achieve a minimum floor to ceiling height of 2.5m, substantially below the required 75%. The resulting low ceiling height across the overwhelming majority of the dwelling would create a compressed internal environment detrimental to the quality and comfort of the accommodation, contrary to Policy D6(F)(8) of the London Plan (2021) and Policies 53, 56 and 57 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).",
    "The submitted Outline Construction Logistics Plan fails to demonstrate safe and practicable construction access and loading arrangements, having regard to the waiting and loading restrictions on Hoe Street, high pedestrian footfall and adjoining cycle track. Consequently, the proposal has not demonstrated that unacceptable obstruction and risks to highway users would be avoided. These fundamental matters require resolution before determination and cannot appropriately be deferred to a condition. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy 64 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024) and Policy T7 of the London Plan (2021)."
  ],
